<!--meta {"lead": "The footer closes every HairPop screen with the brand line and the legal links people look for at the bottom: Terms and Privacy.", "description": "Site footer with brand line and a list of secondary links; wraps on phones.", "pills": ["<code>&lt;footer&gt;</code> landmark", "Status: stable"], "variants": "simple (brand line + legal links), with help and cookie links", "states": "link default, hover, focus, active", "sources": ["pages/style-gallery/default", "pages/terms/default", "pages/privacy/default"]} -->
<section class="ds-section" id="overview"><h2><a href="#overview">Overview</a></h2>
  <p>The footer sits at the end of <code>.product-shell</code> on every product page. It holds the brand line ("HairPop · Made for confident hair decisions") and secondary destinations that must always be findable but never compete with the task: Terms, Privacy and, as the product grows, Help and Cookie preferences.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Do not repeat the primary navigation here; the <a href="top-bar.html">top bar</a> owns it.</li>
    <li>Do not put actions in the footer; a link that opens a dialog (Cookie preferences) is the only exception.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="anatomy"><h2><a href="#anatomy">Anatomy</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-anatomy">
    <figure class="ds-anatomy__figure" style="place-items: stretch; padding: var(--space-8) var(--space-4);">
      <footer class="site-footer" style="width: 100%;"><p>HairPop · Made for confident hair decisions</p><ul class="site-footer__links"><li><a href="../../mocks/pages/terms/default.html">Terms</a></li><li><a href="../../mocks/pages/privacy/default.html">Privacy</a></li></ul></footer>
      <span class="ds-callout" style="left: 8%; top: 18%;" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
      <span class="ds-callout" style="left: 84%; top: 18%;" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
      <span class="ds-callout" style="left: 50%; top: 80%;" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
    </figure>
    <ol class="ds-anatomy__list">
      <li><div><b>Brand line</b><small>One sentence in <code>--text-body-sm</code>, <code>--color-fg-muted</code>.</small></div></li>
      <li><div><b>Links</b><small><code>.site-footer__links</code>: a list of underlined links, 24px tall targets, 16px apart.</small></div></li>
      <li><div><b>Container</b><small>Top hairline <code>--color-border-default</code>, padding <code>--space-6</code> by <code>--layout-margin</code>; wraps with <code>--space-3</code> gaps.</small></div></li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="variants"><h2><a href="#variants">Variants</a></h2>
  {{example:[stack]Simple (today's mocks) and with help and cookie links (recommended once the cookie banner ships).}}
<footer class="site-footer"><p>HairPop · Made for confident hair decisions</p><ul class="site-footer__links"><li><a href="../../mocks/pages/terms/default.html">Terms</a></li><li><a href="../../mocks/pages/privacy/default.html">Privacy</a></li></ul></footer>
<footer class="site-footer"><p>HairPop · Made for confident hair decisions</p><ul class="site-footer__links"><li><a href="../../mocks/pages/help/default.html">Help</a></li><li><a href="../../mocks/dialogs/cookie-preferences/default.html">Cookie preferences</a></li><li><a href="../../mocks/pages/terms/default.html">Terms</a></li><li><a href="../../mocks/pages/privacy/default.html">Privacy</a></li></ul></footer>
  {{/example}}
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="sizes" data-na="The footer has one size; its padding follows --layout-margin per breakpoint."><h2><a href="#sizes">Sizes</a></h2></section>

<section class="ds-section" id="states"><h2><a href="#states">States</a></h2>
  <p>Only the links have states. Forced with <code>data-state</code> here.</p>
  <div class="ds-matrix"><table>
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Element</th><th scope="col">Default</th><th scope="col">Hover</th><th scope="col">Focus</th><th scope="col">Active</th><th scope="col">Visited</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><th scope="row">Footer link</th>
        <td><div class="site-footer" style="border: 0; padding: 0;"><a href="../../mocks/pages/terms/default.html">Terms</a></div></td>
        <td><div class="site-footer" style="border: 0; padding: 0;"><a href="../../mocks/pages/terms/default.html" style="color: var(--color-fg-default); text-decoration-thickness: var(--border-width-thick);">Terms</a></div></td>
        <td><div class="site-footer" style="border: 0; padding: 0;"><a href="../../mocks/pages/terms/default.html" data-state="focus">Terms</a></div></td>
        <td><div class="site-footer" style="border: 0; padding: 0;"><a href="../../mocks/pages/terms/default.html" style="color: var(--color-fg-default);">Terms</a></div></td>
        <td><div class="site-footer" style="border: 0; padding: 0;"><a href="../../mocks/pages/terms/default.html">Terms</a></div></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <p>Footer links inherit the muted colour and turn to the default text colour on hover; visited links look the same as unvisited ones because the set is small and stable. Footer links are never disabled.</p>
  <h3>Both themes</h3>
  {{themes:stack}}<footer class="site-footer" style="padding-inline: 0;"><p>HairPop · Made for confident hair decisions</p><ul class="site-footer__links"><li><a href="../../mocks/pages/terms/default.html">Terms</a></li><li><a href="../../mocks/pages/privacy/default.html">Privacy</a></li></ul></footer>{{/themes}}
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="responsive"><h2><a href="#responsive">Responsive behaviour</a></h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Below about 560px</b> the brand line and the links wrap onto two lines, both left-aligned; the links themselves wrap as a row with 4px row gaps.</li>
    <li><b>Wider</b>, the brand line sits left and the links right on one line (<code>justify-content: space-between</code>).</li>
    <li>Side padding follows <code>--layout-margin</code> so the footer lines up with the page content and the top bar.</li>
    <li>On pages with a fixed bottom element (toasts, cookie banner), the footer keeps its own space; fixed elements add <code>env(safe-area-inset-bottom)</code> and never cover footer links when focused.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="theming"><h2><a href="#theming">Theming</a></h2>
  <p>The footer reads <code>--color-fg-muted</code> (text and links), <code>--color-fg-default</code> (link hover) and <code>--color-border-default</code> (top rule). It sits on the canvas, not a surface, so in the dark theme it is grey 350 text on the grey 950 canvas with a grey 750 rule.</p>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="accessibility"><h2><a href="#accessibility">Accessibility</a></h2>
  <h3>Role and pattern</h3>
  <p><code>&lt;footer class="site-footer"&gt;</code> as a direct child of the shell (outside <code>&lt;main&gt;</code>) is the page's contentinfo landmark. Links sit in a <code>&lt;ul&gt;</code> so screen readers announce "list, 2 items". No ARIA needed.</p>
  <h3>Keyboard</h3>
  <table class="ds-table ds-keys"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Key</th><th scope="col">Action</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td><kbd>Tab</kbd> / <kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>Tab</kbd></td><td>Reaches the footer links last, in visual order.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><kbd>Enter</kbd></td><td>Follows the link (or opens the cookie preferences dialog).</td></tr>
  </tbody></table>
  <h3>Focus</h3>
  <p>The shared 2px ring with 2px offset. Fixed toasts and banners must not obscure a focused footer link (WCAG 2.4.11).</p>
  <h3>Labelling</h3>
  <p>Link text is the destination's name ("Privacy", "Terms"), matching the page's <code>&lt;h1&gt;</code> ("Privacy at HairPop", "Terms of use"). The decorative "·" separators of the mocks are not needed once links are a list.</p>
  <h3>Contrast</h3>
  <div class="ds-example__canvas ds-example__canvas--stack" style="padding: 0; gap: var(--space-2);">
    {{pair:Footer text and links on page|--color-fg-muted|--color-bg-canvas|4.5}}
    {{pair:Hovered link|--color-fg-default|--color-bg-canvas|4.5}}
    {{pair:Focus ring on page|--color-focus-ring|--color-bg-canvas|3}}
  </div>
  <h3>Motion</h3>
  <p>None; colour changes are instant.</p>
  <h3>Touch</h3>
  <p>Links are at least 24px tall (<code>--target-min</code>) with 16px between them horizontally and 4px between wrapped rows; the wrapped rows remain 24px apart edge to edge because each target is 24px tall.</p>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="content"><h2><a href="#content">Content</a></h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The brand line stays "HairPop · Made for confident hair decisions" everywhere.</li>
    <li>Link labels are one or two words in sentence case: "Terms", "Privacy", "Cookie preferences", "Help".</li>
    <li>Order: Help, Cookie preferences, Terms, Privacy. Never more than six links.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="do-dont"><h2><a href="#do-dont">Do and don't</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-dodont">
    <figure class="ds-do"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><footer class="site-footer" style="width: 100%;"><p>HairPop · Made for confident hair decisions</p><ul class="site-footer__links"><li><a href="../../mocks/pages/terms/default.html">Terms</a></li><li><a href="../../mocks/pages/privacy/default.html">Privacy</a></li></ul></footer></div><figcaption>Put footer links in a list; spacing comes from the list, not glyphs.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-dont"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><footer class="site-footer" style="width: 100%;"><span>HairPop · Made for confident hair decisions</span><span><a href="../../mocks/pages/terms/default.html">Terms</a> · <a href="../../mocks/pages/privacy/default.html">Privacy</a></span></footer></div><figcaption>Separate links with a "·" text glyph inside one span, as the mocks do; the dot is read aloud and the targets crowd together.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-do"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><p class="text-muted">Help · Cookie preferences · Terms · Privacy</p></div><figcaption>Give people a way back to cookie preferences after they dismiss the banner.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-dont"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><p class="text-muted">Styles · Braiders · Appointments · Help · Terms · Privacy</p></div><figcaption>Repeat the primary navigation in the footer.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="tokens"><h2><a href="#tokens">Tokens</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-table-wrap"><table class="ds-table">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Part</th><th scope="col">Token</th><th scope="col">Light</th><th scope="col">Dark</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {{tok:Text and links|--color-fg-muted}}
      {{tok:Link hover|--color-fg-default}}
      {{tok:Top rule|--color-border-default}}
      {{tok:Background|--color-bg-canvas}}
      {{tok:Padding block / inline|--space-6|--layout-margin}}
      {{tok:Gap|--space-3}}
      {{tok:Link gap|--space-1|--space-4}}
      {{tok:Link target|--target-min}}
      {{tok:Font|--text-body-sm}}
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="code"><h2><a href="#code">Code</a></h2>
  <pre><code>&lt;footer class="site-footer"&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;HairPop · Made for confident hair decisions&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;ul class="site-footer__links"&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="/terms"&gt;Terms&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="/privacy"&gt;Privacy&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
  &lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/footer&gt;</code></pre>
  <table class="ds-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Class / attribute</th><th scope="col">Effect</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td><code>.site-footer</code></td><td>Wrapping row with top rule, muted small text; <code>.footer</code> is an alias.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>.site-footer__links</code></td><td>Unstyled list laid out as a wrapping row.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>data-state="focus"</code></td><td>Documentation only.</td></tr>
  </tbody></table>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="sources"><h2><a href="#sources">Sources</a></h2>
  <ul>
    {{mock:pages/style-gallery/default|footer on every product page}}
    {{mock:pages/terms/default|Terms destination}}
    {{mock:pages/privacy/default|Privacy destination}}
  </ul>
  <p>Drift fixed during extraction: links were plain anchors in a <code>&lt;span&gt;</code> separated by a "·" glyph (system uses a list); the kit had two footers, <code>.footer</code> and <code>.site-footer</code>, with different padding (merged, <code>.footer</code> kept as an alias); there was no route back to cookie preferences after the consent banner (system recommends a footer link).</p>
</section>
